# `compiler` by the mechanical rule red set on BatteryReorg (cites nothing,
# carries a machine sidecar), and the rule's REASON does not hold for this one:
# it is named here so nobody reads the label as the claim.
#
# The sibling smp-* arms take `compiler` because "no kernel or board change can
# break it". This arm is about the BED. It goes red on a change to
# `tools/codex-vm.c`, which no battery selects on, so `compiler` is where it
# runs rather than what it is about. Verified falsifiable both ways 2026-09-07:
# the pre-fix codex-vm (#120) prints AP DISAGREES WITH BSP and the fixed one
# prints ap agrees with bsp, on the same binary of the subject.
compiler
